  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: af6c11f0d531f4249801ea5c2de41bcb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ReadableTrigger
  interactionPrompt: Read
  backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5face2da520a6fa4fa8eff1c614aff70, type: 3}
  fontOverride: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
  overrideAlignment: 0
  textAlignment: 257
  overrideMargins: 0
  textMargins: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  overrideLineSpacing: 0
  lineSpacing: 0
  overrideFontSize: 1
  fontSize: 18
  overrideFontColor: 0
  fontColor: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  pages:
  - "Recovered Field Note, Informal Designation: \n\u201CThe Beast\u201D\nSource
    redacted\n\nSurvivors agree on this much: the creature does not announce itself.
    It waits until it has judged you. Signs of weakness of mind appear to draw it
    closer. It watches for hesitation. For the moment your thoughts slow and your
    will folds inward.\n\nThose who never realize they were being hunted often report
    nothing at all. They vanish quietly. No screams or signs of pursuit. The Beast
    does not waste energy on panic."
  - 'When it does show itself, it is deliberate and brief. A silhouette where there
    should be none.


    It favors concealment over speed, patience over force.
    It will remain unseen for hours, sometimes days, tracking the same individual
    until the prey convinces it - through fear, isolation, or doubt, that the kill
    will be effortless.


    Those who stare at it lose their mind. It is also known
    to interfere with electronic equipment.'
  enableLowSanityOverride: 0
  lowSanityThreshold: 0.25
