  fontColor: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  pages:
  - 'The Watchman''s Notes

    1999'
  - In this book you will find instructions on how to watch over this graveyard.
    Do not deviate from these instructions. This book contains a compilation of all
    recordings from previous grave watchers.
  - This resting place is centuries old and should not be tampered with.  As the
    gravekeeper, you will read the following instructions and abide by them.
  - You must only allow for visitors who are directly related to the deceased.
  - Do not blindly trust visitors. Always cross reference any information they provide
    you.
  - You will stand guard at the gate to prevent unwanted visitors from tampering
    with the gravesites. You must also patrol the grounds.
  - If someone is trespassing, use your flashlight to deter them.
  - 'Ensure that the lights are on at all times throughout the graveyard. '
  - Do not shine your flashlight directly onto the tombstones.
  - Ensure that the crucifix is properly affixed onto the door of the cabin at all
    times. The crucifix will determine your sanity.
  enableLowSanityOverride: 0
