--- !u!114 &1236936888
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1236936884}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: af6c11f0d531f4249801ea5c2de41bcb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ReadableTrigger
  interactionPrompt: Read
  backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5face2da520a6fa4fa8eff1c614aff70, type: 3}
  fontOverride: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
  overrideAlignment: 0
  textAlignment: 272
  overrideMargins: 0
  textMargins: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  overrideLineSpacing: 0
  lineSpacing: 0
  overrideFontSize: 1
  fontSize: 18
  overrideFontColor: 1
  fontColor: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 1}
  pages:
  - "Excerpt from the Gravekeeper\u2019s Notes\nHuang family\n\nFamily members:\nWenqi
    Huang, 73, Alive\nMei Huang, 70, Deceased\nChen Huang, 48, Alive\n\nMei Haung
    is interred within these grounds.\n\nCause of death: Lethal injection\n\nTime
    of death: March 27, 1993, Saturday 4:00 PM"
  - "There is only one grave under the Huang name, though the arrangements suggest
    a decision made in haste and upheld with care. The plot was chosen by Huang Wenqi
    himself; he arrived with the paperwork prepared and spoke clearly, though not
    always consistently, occasionally repeating details already settled. Madam Huang
    was brought at dawn. No extended family attended. When I asked whether the son
    would come, Wenqi said the family was complete as it stood, then paused, as if
    uncertain why the answer mattered. The cause of death was recorded, a crime resolved,
    and the matter accepted without dispute.\n\nMei Huang lived quietly, known for
    small kindnesses that left little record. In her final months, that attention
    faded, and with it her protection. I was told only that a matter of dishonor
    had been resolved; no details were given. No offerings are permitted in the son\u2019s
    name. Wenqi visits alone now, sometimes repeating himself, always checking the
    stone before leaving, as if expecting it to say something different."
  enableLowSanityOverride: 0
  lowSanityThreshold: 0.25
  lowSanityOverrides:
    overridePages: 0
    pages: []
    overrideBackground: 0
    backgroundImage: {fileID: 0}
    fontOverride: {fileID: 0}
    overrideAlignment: 0
    textAlignment: 257
    overrideMargins: 0
    textMargins: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
    overrideLineSpacing: 0
    lineSpacing: 0
    overrideFontSize: 0
    fontSize: 24
    overrideFontColor: 0
    fontColor: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
    enableShake: 0
    shakeIntensity: 2
    shakeSpeed: 25
