--- !u!114 &1770896530
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1770896528}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: af6c11f0d531f4249801ea5c2de41bcb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ReadableTrigger
  interactionPrompt: Read
  backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5face2da520a6fa4fa8eff1c614aff70, type: 3}
  fontOverride: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
  overrideAlignment: 0
  textAlignment: 257
  overrideMargins: 0
  textMargins: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  overrideLineSpacing: 0
  lineSpacing: 0
  overrideFontSize: 1
  fontSize: 18
  overrideFontColor: 0
  fontColor: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  pages:
  - "Recovered Field Note, Provisional Designation:\n\u201CThe Grave Robber\u201D\nSource
    redacted\n\nA recurring human presence has been connected to the majority of
    grave disturbances. The individual is believed to be a local resident who acts
    as the primary point of contact for outsiders engaging in theft and desecration.
    His true identity remains unknown.\n\nHe does not work alone. His accomplices
    are frequently observed scouting the cemetery during off hours, testing sightlines
    and response times. These individuals retreat when illuminated and have been
    successfully deterred with sustained use of flashlights. Constant vigilance is
    required, as their activity is ongoing and deliberate."
  - 'Foreigners arrive with detailed knowledge of the cemetery layout, patrol patterns,
    and access routes, despite having no prior connection to the area. This information
    is presumed to be supplied by him. Activity increases sharply following his arrival
    and disperses once he leaves.


    The Grave Robber is violent. Evidence suggests
    intentional intimidation rather than necessity. Damaged tools, excessive force,
    and signs of internal conflict among accomplices indicate a leadership role maintained
    through fear.


    Previous gravekeepers have reported encounters. In each case,
    documentation ends shortly afterward. One keeper abandoned the post without notice.
    Another was hospitalized with injuries inconsistent with a fall. A third recorded
    a sighting but the final entry was torn from the log.'
  - He avoids identification. Facial details vary between reports, and no reliable
    image has been captured. Despite this, his presence is unmistakable. Continued
    observation is necessary. Direct confrontation is not advised.
  enableLowSanityOverride: 0
  lowSanityThreshold: 0.25
  lowSanityOverrides:
